---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Contact GuideHollow" description="Report a broken link, suggest an article correction, or ask a question about GuideHollow through GuideHollow’s available contact channels." breadcrumbs={[{name:'Contact',url:'/contact/'}]}>
<header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow mint">/ contact</p><h1>Help make the path clearer.</h1><p>Found a mistake, a broken link, or a question our guides should answer? Let us know.</p></header><article class="prose info-content">{site.contactEmail && <section><h2>Private correspondence</h2><p>For a private question, <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>email GuideHollow</a>. Your chosen email provider handles the message. Share only the details needed for your request and never send passwords or API keys.</p></section>}<h2>Send a correction or question</h2><p>Our current public contact channel is the GuideHollow GitHub issue tracker. A GitHub account is required to submit an issue. You can read existing issues without signing in.</p><p><a class="button primary" href={site.contact}>Open a GitHub issue ↗</a></p><p><a href={`${site.repository}/issues`}>View existing issues</a></p><h2>What to include</h2><ul><li>The URL and title of the page.</li><li>The sentence or feature that needs attention.</li><li>What you expected and what happened.</li><li>An official reference if you are suggesting a factual correction.</li></ul><h2>Keep personal information out of public issues</h2><p>Issues are public. Do not post passwords, API keys, personal documents, private account details, or other sensitive information. For a privacy question, describe the request without sharing the underlying personal data.</p><p>{site.contactEmail ? 'There is no contact form on this site. Use email for correspondence you do not want to post publicly.' : 'We do not currently publish a private email contact or operate a contact form. If you need private correspondence, do not submit confidential information to the public tracker.'} No response time is guaranteed.</p></article>
</Base>
